---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Panel from '../../components/Panel.astro';
import FieldStrip from '../../components/FieldStrip.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="4th down calculator"
  description="Set any 4th down situation and compare the win probability of going for it against kicking."
>
  <h1 class="page-title">4th down calculator</h1>
  <div class="content-grid">
    <Panel title="Example situation">
      <FieldStrip ballOn={58} lineToGain={61} label="4th & 3 at DET 42" />
      <p class="explain">
        The strip reads left to right: the chalk line is the ball, the yellow line is the first
        down, and the shaded gap is the distance. When the calculator is live, you will set the
        spot, distance, score, and clock, and this page will show the win probability for each
        choice.
      </p>
    </Panel>
    <Panel title="Status">
      <p>
        The model is being trained and is not on this page yet. The site around it is real: the
        interface it will plug into is defined, and graded calls will feed the record in the
        sidebar.
      </p>
    </Panel>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .explain {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 60ch;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
</style>
